{
  "title": "Burners & Stingers",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/knee-and-sports/3115/burners-and-stingers",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Sep 11 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Burners and stingers (also known as \"dead arm syndrome\") refer to a transient brachial plexus neuropraxia that most commonly occur due to a direct traumatic or tractional injury in contact sports.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with a neurological examination most commonly consistent of unilateral tingling in the arm with transient weakness in C5, C6 muscles (deltoid, biceps).",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is typically observation and return to play if symptoms completely resolve. Players are not allowed to return to play in the setting of persistent or bilateral symptoms.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "common in collision sports such as football",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "having 1 stinger increases risk of another by 3X",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathoanatomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**neurapraxias are caused by different mechanisms including**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**traction injury**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "occurs by downward displacement of arm and bending of neck away from side of injury",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**compression injury**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "occurs by lateral head turning toward affected side",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**direct blow**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "can cause injury with blow at Erb's point superior to the clavicle",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Brachial plexus**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "with motor and sensory innervation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3115/images/Brachial%20Plexus%20with%20sensory%20566_moved.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**unilateral tingling** in arm not typically isolated to a single dermatome",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "usually resolve quickly in 1-2 minutes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "full cervical ROM",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "no tenderness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "unilateral **transient weakness** in C5, C6 muscles (deltoid, biceps)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "can have positive Spurling test",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually unremarkable",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "C-spine images **indicated with recurring symptoms**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "to rule out fx and cervical stenosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indicated whenever symptoms are **bilateral** (inconsistent with stinger)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "to rule out cervical spine pathology such as herniated disc or cervical stenosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "EMG",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indicated if symptoms persist after 3 weeks",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "will show abnormalities in roots, cords, trunks, and peripheral nerves",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "return to play",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "a player may return to play when",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**complete resolution of symptoms**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**normal strength and range of motion**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "contraindications to return to play include",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**bilateral symptoms**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "multiple stingers",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "until further off-field workup is completed",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "-1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**recurring symptoms**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "until cervical spine xrays are obtained",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Prevention",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "try different neck collars for football players",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
